  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Scattered early morning showers quickly give way to \nplenty of sunshine, breezy and unseasonable warm high temps well \ninto the 80s today.\n\nScattered showers early this morning will quickly exit the coastal \nplain by early-mid morning. Otherwise...westerly flow aloft and at \nthe surface will allow skies to become mostly sunny by late morning-\nearly afternoon. Post frontal airmass still quite warm with 925T on \nthe order of +22C to +24C. This coupled with lots of sunshine and \nwesterly flow should allow highs to reach the middle 80s in many \nlocations with even a few upper 80s possible. Bufkit soundings also \nindicate good mixing...so expect westerly wind gusts on the order of \n20 to 30 mph with a few gusts near 35 mph across parts MA especially \nthe higher terrain. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Plenty of sunshine with comfortable humidity Fri-\nSat. Highs mainly in the 70s. Lows Fri night in the 40s-lower 50s. \n\nLarge high pressure builds in from the west Fri into Sat. This will \nresult in absolutely beautiful September weather. Plenty of sunshine \nwith highs mainly in the middle to upper 70s both days with very \ncomfortable humidity. Mainly clear skies, light winds, and a dry \nairmass in place will allow for a good night of radiational cooling \nFriday night. Lows Fri night should mainly be in the 40s to the \nlower 50s and 55-60 in the Urban Heat Island of Boston. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...Period of showers likely sometime late Sat night \ninto Sun with perhaps some downpours. Dry & seasonable weather \nfollows Mon. \n\nHigh pressure moves off the coast for the second half of the weekend \nallowing a shortwave and associated mid-level warm front to \napproach. This will likely bring a period of showers sometime late \nSat night and/or Sun. Pwats reach around 2 inches so some downpours \nare possible too...especially if there is a low level boundary in \nplace. Some of the guidance indicates this potential near and south \nof the MA Turnpike...so something to watch over the next few days. \n\nA ridge of high pressure should return by Monday...bringing mainly \ndry and seasonable weather for the start of the next work week. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 4...Unseasonable warmth may return for a day or two by \nthe middle of next week ahead of our next cold front.\n\nAn anomalous upper level ridge of high ridge will build across the \nsoutheast states during the first half of next week. This will \nresult in west to southwest flow aloft and above normal height \nfields across southern New England. We will have to see how much \nsouthwest flow/mixing we can generate at the surface ahead of the \nnext cold front. But given the setup...there is the potential for \nhighs to reach back into the 80s for a day or two by the middle of \nnext week ahead of the next cold front.",
